---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<Layout title="Privacy | Pranjal Pandey" description="How this website handles newsletter signups, guide requests, booking links and privacy questions.">
  <div class="wrap privacy-page"><header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Privacy / Updated 19 October 2026</p><h1>Your email is not a trade-off.</h1></header>
    <section class="privacy-summary" aria-labelledby="privacy-summary-title">
      <h2 id="privacy-summary-title">The short version</h2>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <div class="card"><h3>What I collect</h3><p>Your email if you sign up. Analytics and advertising providers also process page visits, clicks and technical identifiers.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>What I don't</h3><p>This site's code does not send your signup email to analytics or advertising tags. Booking providers handle payment details.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Your controls</h3><p>Turn tracking off below, unsubscribe using the link in any letter, or <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>email me</a> to request deletion of your subscriber data.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="doc-layout">
      <nav class="doc-toc" aria-label="Privacy sections">
        <a href="#reading-site">Reading this site</a><a href="#tracking">Analytics & advertising</a><a href="#tracking-settings">Tracking settings</a><a href="#guides-letter">Guides & letter</a><a href="#bookings">Bookings</a><a href="#email">Email</a><a href="#changes">Changes</a>
      </nav>
      <div class="doc-prose"><p>This personal website is operated by Pranjal Pandey. For privacy questions or requests, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
      <section id="reading-site"><h2>Reading this site</h2><p>The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub may process request information, including IP addresses, to serve and protect the website. See <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's privacy statement ↗</a>. Fonts and the portrait are served with the website, not requested from Google Fonts.</p></section>
      <section id="tracking">
      <h2>Analytics & advertising</h2>
      <p>Google Analytics 4, the LinkedIn Insight Tag and the Meta Pixel load by default on the live website. They can use cookies and process page visits, device and browser information, and network identifiers to measure traffic, understand campaigns and support advertising audiences. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy ↗</a>, <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/legal/privacy-policy">LinkedIn's privacy policy ↗</a> and <a href="https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy/">Meta's privacy policy ↗</a>.</p>
      <p>Visits to the guides' signup and confirmation pages are measured as page visits, not proof that an email was confirmed. Guide download choices and booking-link clicks are measured to understand what readers find useful, not to verify downloads, bookings or payments. Site code does not send your signup email address to these tags.</p>
      </section>
      <section id="tracking-settings">
        <h2>Tracking settings</h2>
        <div class="tracking-settings card">
          <label for="tracking-switch"><span>Analytics & ad measurement</span><input class="switch" id="tracking-switch" type="checkbox" role="switch" aria-describedby="tracking-explanation tracking-status" disabled /></label>
          <p id="tracking-explanation">Allow Google Analytics, LinkedIn and Meta tracking on this browser. Changes save automatically and reload this page to apply.</p>
          <p class="fine-print" role="status" id="tracking-status"></p>
        </div>
      <noscript><p>These analytics tags do not load without JavaScript.</p></noscript>
      <p>Your choice is stored on this browser and applies on subsequent page loads. Disabling tracking stops these tags from loading; it does not delete information already sent or cookies already set. You can remove existing cookies in your browser settings. Kit, hosting and external booking providers are separate from this preference.</p>
      </section>
      <section id="guides-letter"><h2>The guides and monthly letter</h2><p>If you request either free guide, your email address is submitted to the same Kit form to handle confirmation and delivery, and to send <em>Practical AI</em>, my monthly letter with a business section and a section for individuals. No separate audience tag is applied by this website. The signup page states this before you submit.</p><p>Kit's form script loads on pages with an inline signup. It can process technical request and form-interaction information. See <a href="https://kit.com/privacy">Kit's privacy policy ↗</a>. A guide confirmation or delivery message is additional to the monthly letter.</p><p>You can unsubscribe using the link in an email, or contact me for help. I keep subscriber information while you remain subscribed or as needed to handle your request and meet applicable obligations. You can ask to access, correct or delete your information by email; necessary records may be retained where required.</p></section>
      <section id="bookings"><h2>Bookings and paid sessions</h2><p>Booking links take you to Cal.com or Topmate. Those providers handle the information you submit, scheduling and any payment. This website does not collect payment card details. Check <a href="https://cal.com/privacy">Cal.com's privacy policy ↗</a> and <a href="https://topmate.io/privacy">Topmate's privacy policy ↗</a> before booking.</p></section>
      <section id="email"><h2>Email and confidential information</h2><p>If you email me, I use your message to respond and manage the conversation. Please don't send private client data, credentials or sensitive materials in an initial enquiry.</p></section>
      <section id="changes"><h2>Changes</h2><p>This notice will be updated if the website changes how it uses personal information.</p></section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
<script>
  import '../scripts/tracking-settings';
</script>
